    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d165">

                <pb facs="0247" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg181"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3731/1036: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the President of Cuba</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Mendieta</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-29">August 29, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personally and on behalf of the people and Government of the United States I
                    desire warmly to reciprocate the cordial sentiments expressed in Your
                    Excellency’s message on the occasion of the signing of the trade agreement
                    between the United States and Cuba.</p>
                <p>This readjustment of the basis upon which the commercial relations between our
                    respective countries have rested since the Convention of 1902 to meet the
                    necessities of present-day conditions has been achieved in an exemplary spirit
                    of amity and close cooperation.</p>
                <p>It is my conviction, not only that the United States and Cuba will immediately
                    feel the beneficial effects of this agreement in increased exchange of products
                    to their mutual general advantage, but that the conclusion of this agreement may
                    serve to initiate a widespread movement toward general reduction of those
                    artificial barriers which have so largely contributed to stagnation of
                    international trade.</p>
                <p>I am particularly happy to have been associated with Your Excellency in this
                    achievement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Franklin D.
                    Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
